title: Proposition 24
---
order: 24
---
short_label: I.24
---
sections:

#### prop_section ####
kind: proposition
----
statement: If two triangles have two sides equal to two sides respectively, but have one of the angles contained by the equal straight lines greater than the other, then they also have the base greater than the base.
----
proof:

Let {ABC} and {DEF} be two triangles having the two sides {AB} and {AC} equal to the two sides {DE} and {DF} respectively, so that {AB} equals {DE}, and {AC} equals {DF}, and let the angle at {A} be greater than the angle at {D}.

I say that the base {BC} is greater than the base {EF}.

